WEBVTT

0
00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:06.500
Sprezzature is an AI engine for Design.
UI does the half a command can do.

1
00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:10.987
It finds your translatable sentences.
Then it writes the catalogue.

2
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:17.162
A sentence written into a template
costs nothing on the day you write it.

3
00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:22.119
It costs a week the day somebody
needs a second language.

4
00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:27.337
And prompts are language too.
A missing one, the model answers.

5
00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:34.040
It looks for 2 shapes and names them.
Not for every literal.

6
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:40.480
A locale table living in JavaScript.
A model prompt inlined in Python.

7
00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:46.599
Any finding and it returns one.
That is what makes it a pre-commit hook.

8
00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:52.280
Only you know which id that line wants.
So it stops, as gettext does.

9
00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:57.720
Now the part you would not guess.
A prompt is not an interface label.

10
00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:03.120
It has one language it was tested in,
and the catalogue declares it.

11
00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:09.200
A locale with no entry falls back to it.
Never to the message id.

12
00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:15.250
Nobody published that rule.
The package has a test that measured it.

13
00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:24.400
Here is the file it writes.
Interface labels on top, prompts below.

14
00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:31.440
Both kinds in one file. A screen
and a prompt disagreeing is a silent bug.

15
00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:37.960
At the bottom, one key: validated.
No label above it needs that.

16
00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:47.800
Go to sprezzature.ai,
and drop a GitHub star if it deserves it.

17
00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:53.000
Make it, audit it, take a look at it.
